# Kowalski 2020, example (1): the rock-paper-scissors reactive rule, with the
# static beats relation as declarative facts.
#
# The paper's sentence is reproduced verbatim except for two noun phrases whose
# referent lives outside the clause -- 'the game' and 'the prize' -- which the
# paper leaves to its cross-sentence context.  v1 has no cross-sentence
# anaphora, so they are declared constants ([names] RpsGame / RpsPrize): a
# loud, declared reading rather than a guessed one (see README, gap g1).

Rock beats Scissors.
Scissors beats Paper.
Paper beats Rock.

If a player P1 plays a choice C1 and another player P2 plays a choice C2 and C1 beats C2 and it is not the case that RpsGame is over then P1 receives RpsPrize and it becomes the case that RpsGame is over.
